{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nMr. Chanek has an integer represented by a string $$$s$$$. Zero or more digits have been erased and are denoted by the character _. There are also zero or more digits marked by the character X, meaning they're the same digit.Mr. Chanek wants to count the number of possible integer $$$s$$$, where $$$s$$$ is divisible by $$$25$$$. Of course, $$$s$$$ must not contain any leading zero. He can replace the character _ with any digit. He can also replace the character X with any digit, but it must be the same for every character X.As a note, a leading zero is any 0 digit that comes before the first nonzero digit in a number string in positional notation. For example, 0025 has two leading zeroes. An exception is the integer zero, (0 has no leading zero, but 0000 has three leading zeroes).\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        FastReader input = new FastReader();\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        int T = 1;\n        while (T-- > 0) {\n            String s = input.next();\n            if (s.length() == 1) {\n                out.println(isSpecialChar(s.charAt(0)) ? 1 : 0);\n            } else {\n                if (!s.contains(\"X\")) {\n                    out.println(countValid(s));\n                } else {\n                    int sum = 0;\n                    for (int d = 0; d < 10; d++) {\n                        sum += countValid(s.replace(\"X\", String.valueOf(d)));\n                    }\n                    out.println(sum);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    private static boolean isSpecialChar(char c) {\n        return c == '0' || c == '_' || c == 'X';\n    }\n\n    public static int countValid(String s) {\n        int n = s.length();\n        int prefix = (s.charAt(0) == '0') ? 0 : 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {\n            if (s.charAt(i) == '_') {\n                prefix *= (i == 0) ? 9 : 10;\n            }\n        }\n        int suffix = 0;\n        char c1 = s.charAt(n - 2);\n        char c2 = s.charAt(n - 1);\n        if (c1 == '_' && c2 == '_') {\n            suffix = 4;\n        } else if (c2 == '_') {\n            if (c1 == '0' || c1 == '5' || c1 == '2' || c1 == '7') {\n                suffix = 1;\n            }\n        } else if (c1 == '_') {\n            if (c2 == '0' || c2 == '5') {\n                suffix = 2;\n            }\n        } else {\n            int val = Integer.parseInt(s.substring(n - 2));\n            suffix = (val % 25 == 0) ? 1 : 0;\n        }\n        return prefix * suffix;\n    }\n\n    static class FastReader {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        public FastReader() {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        }\n\n        String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreElements()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n\n        String nextLine() {\n            String str = \"\";\n            try {\n                str = br.readLine();\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                e.printStackTrace();\n            }\n            return str;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        FastReader input = new FastReader();\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        int T = 1;\n        while (T-- > 0) {\n            String s = input.next();\n            out.println(countValidNumbers(s));\n        }\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    private static long countValidNumbers(String s) {\n        int n = s.length();\n        \n        // Check if there are any X characters\n        if (s.contains(\"X\")) {\n            long total = 0;\n            for (int d = 0; d <= 9; d++) {\n                String replaced = s.replace(\"X\", String.valueOf(d));\n                total += countValid(replaced);\n            }\n            return total;\n        }\n        \n        return countValid(s);\n    }\n\n    private static long countValid(String s) {\n        int n = s.length();\n        \n        // Check for leading zero issues\n        if (s.charAt(0) == '0' && n > 1) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n        \n        // Count possibilities for positions before the last two digits\n        long prefixCount = 1;\n        boolean hasLeadingUnderscore = (s.charAt(0) == '_');\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {\n            char c = s.charAt(i);\n            if (c == '_') {\n                if (i == 0) {\n                    prefixCount *= 9; // Cannot be 0 for first digit\n                } else {\n                    prefixCount *= 10; // Can be any digit\n                }\n            } else if (c != 'X') {\n                // Fixed digit, no change\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Handle last two digits\n        char c1 = s.charAt(n - 2);\n        char c2 = s.charAt(n - 1);\n        long suffixCount = 0;\n        \n        if (c1 == '_' && c2 == '_') {\n            // Both digits are erased, count valid endings for divisibility by 25\n            suffixCount = 4; // 00, 25, 50, 75\n        } else if (c1 == '_') {\n            // Only first of last two digits is erased\n            if (c2 == '0') {\n                suffixCount = 10; // 00, 10, 20, ..., 90 - but only those divisible by 25: 00, 50\n                // Actually, for divisibility by 25, if last digit is 0, first digit can be 0 or 5\n                suffixCount = 2; // 00, 50\n            } else if (c2 == '5') {\n                suffixCount = 2; // 25, 75\n            } else {\n                suffixCount = 0;\n            }\n        } else if (c2 == '_') {\n            // Only second of last two digits is erased\n            if (c1 == '0') {\n                suffixCount = 1; // 00\n            } else if (c1 == '2') {\n                suffixCount = 1; // 25\n            } else if (c1 == '5') {\n                suffixCount = 1; // 50\n            } else if (c1 == '7') {\n                suffixCount = 1; // 75\n            } else {\n                suffixCount = 0;\n            }\n        } else {\n            // No underscores in last two digits\n            int lastTwo = (c1 - '0') * 10 + (c2 - '0');\n            suffixCount = (lastTwo % 25 == 0) ? 1 : 0;\n        }\n        \n        return prefixCount * suffixCount;\n    }\n\n    static class FastReader {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        public FastReader() {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        }\n\n        String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreElements()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n\n        String nextLine() {\n            String str = \"\";\n            try {\n                str = br.readLine();\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                e.printStackTrace();\n            }\n            return str;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00016962042718660086, -3.2186455882765586e-06, 0.0, -1.3351351299206726e-05, -2.586808113846928e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.0251946150674485e-05, -0.000476246903417632, -1.7523612768854946e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.8265450712060556e-05, -4.291525328881107e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -4.291525328881107e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -5.960446742392378e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.145764938177308e-06, -4.172316494077677e-06, -2.264974000354414e-06, -5.745722592109814e-05, -1.3828182090946939e-05, 0.0, -1.311301275563892e-06, -2.145764938177308e-06, -2.253030106658116e-05, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -5.8412379075889476e-06, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -4.291525328881107e-